WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Spread starlight out by wavelength,
and you might expect a smooth band:

2
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.290
every wavelength, no gaps.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.710
Look closely, though.

4
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.270
Thin dark lines cross it.

5
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.100
Look through a diffraction
grating instead of a prism,

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.540
and the same dark lines appear
again, on both sides of the centre.

7
00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.650
What makes these dark gaps?

8
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.320
And what can they tell us?

9
00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.880
In this mission, you'll see
where a star's light comes from,

10
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.760
and why a grating spreads
it the way it does.

11
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.380
Then you'll line up a star's spectrum
against lines measured in the laboratory.

12
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.600
Your mission: explain
what makes the dark gaps,

13
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:37.800
and what they reveal.
